<div class="wrap">
  <header>
    <div class="eyebrow">02-120 · qPCR primers and SARS-CoV-2</div>
    <h1>qPCR Primer Designer</h1>
    <p class="lede">Paste a genome and a target gene inside it. The designer suggests a forward
      primer, a reverse primer and a probe, ranked best match first, and checks with the
      specificity model that each design makes only one product in the whole genome.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="card">
    <form id="form" novalidate>
      <div class="field">
        <div class="label-row">
          <label for="genome">Genome</label>
          <span class="counter" id="genome-count">0 bases</span>
        </div>
        <textarea id="genome" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste a genome, plain or FASTA (a SARS-CoV-2 genome is about 30,000 bases)"></textarea>
        <div class="actions">
          <input id="genome-file" class="visually-hidden" type="file" accept=".fasta,.fa,.fna,.txt">
          <label for="genome-file" class="btn">Open FASTA file</label>
        </div>
        <div class="examples">
          <span class="hint">Load an example (fills both boxes and runs):</span>
          <div class="actions" id="example-buttons">
            <button type="button" id="example">SARS-CoV-2 N gene</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <div class="label-row">
          <label for="target">Target gene</label>
          <span class="counter" id="target-count">0 bases</span>
        </div>
        <textarea id="target" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste the target gene's sequence; it must appear in the genome (either strand)"></textarea>
      </div>

      <div class="row">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="allowance">Mismatch allowance</label>
          <select id="allowance">
            <option value="0">0</option>
            <option value="1">1</option>
            <option value="2" selected>2</option>
          </select>
          <span class="hint">Off-target sites with this many mismatches or fewer count as binding. Capped at 2 so the search stays complete for 18-base primers.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="product-min">Product length range (bp)</label>
          <div class="range-row">
            <input id="product-min" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="54" step="1" value="60" aria-label="Shortest product (bp)">
            <span class="hint">to</span>
            <input id="product-max" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="54" step="1" value="150" aria-label="Longest product (bp)">
          </div>
          <span class="hint">Designs are only made inside this range, and shorter products rank higher. qPCR works best at 60–150 bp.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="actions">
        <button type="submit" class="primary" id="run">Suggest primers</button>
        <span id="status" role="status"></span>
      </div>
    </form>
  </section>

  <section id="results" aria-live="polite"></section>

  <details class="card">
    <summary>How the designer chooses</summary>
    <ul>
      <li>Primers are 18–24 bases, the probe 18–30. At each position the length with GC closest to 50 % is used.</li>
      <li>Every primer and probe must be 40–60 % GC. The target's GC is checked first: above 70 % stops the design, 60–70 % or below 40 % gives a warning.</li>
      <li>The probe sits in the middle of the gap between the primers.</li>
      <li>Ranking, best match first: penalty = the three oligos' distance from 50 % GC (percentage points) + (product length − shortest allowed) ÷ 10, so shorter products rank higher. Lower is better.</li>
      <li>A design is kept only if each oligo binds exactly once in the whole genome and the first model finds exactly one product, with the probe inside it. Later designs do not overlap earlier ones.</li>
      <li>Not considered: melting temperature, hairpins and primer dimers.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>

  <footer>Positions are 1-based genome coordinates. The reverse primer is shown 3'→5' so it lines up under the genome; order it 5'→3' as listed.</footer>
